<br/>You can expect ~5-6% healing from the two bonuses combined. You will alter your rotation to include Healing Touch when at 5 stacks of the 2pc buff.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Restoration Druid</span></h2>In Phase 5, you can at last finish the Legendary Quest Line and earn your Legendary Cloak. We only have one choice in <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102247/jina-kang-kindness-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Jina-Kang, Kindness of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_cranehealer_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jina-Kang, Kindness of Chi-Ji</span></a>. Over the course of a fight, it puts in a decent amount of work and the effect is very good while active. The only downside is that the proc rate is low and so variance can feel high. You can read more about how to finish the questline and obtain the cloak <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/raids/legendary-cloak-questline-overview">here</a>.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Restoration Druid Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>Phase 5 trinkets are very varied and we have a lot of great choices. They are all passive.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102299/prismatic-prison-of-pride">
<img alt="Prismatic Prison of Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Prismatic Prison of Pride</span></a> <i>(Sha of Pride)</i> - A very powerful trinket that replaces typical passive intellect with an interesting secondary stat amplification. It lets us hit breakpoints more easily, and greatly increases the amount of Spirit and Mastery we'll have. This is a lock for your first trinket slot.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102309/dysmorphic-samophlange-of-discontinuity">
<img alt="Dysmorphic Samophlange of Discontinuity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dysmorphic Samophlange of Discontinuity</span></a> <i>(Siegecrafted Blackfuse)</i> - The raids premier regeneration trinket. This is the most straightforward choice for your second trinket slot, and has the least variance, though it also has much smaller peaks than the alternatives below.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102304/thoks-acid-grooved-tooth">
<img alt="Thok's Acid-Grooved Tooth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Acid-Grooved Tooth</span></a> <i>(Thok the Bloodthirsty)</i> - While the cleave effect is absurdly strong on paper, it has a very small range. You will likely find this trinket is situationally your best-in-slot, but dependent on how stacked your raid is. The cleave will duplicate the entire heal, and works on all of our healing except some Force of Nature abilities.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
